      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have been meaning to check and see what headers are sent. \n\nI think since Accept exists, it should be used instead of making a new one. https://webmasters.stackexchange.com/questions/31212/difference-between-the-accept-and-content-type-http-headers\n\nAlso X-VRCHAT-ACCEPT would be more proper. Still not a good idea to define a parameter where one exists.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-02-26T17:06:18.181Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, the server side accessed from a text / image downloader cannot determine whether the access is from a text downloader or an image downloader from the user-agent or other header information. If it can be determined, the same URL can be used by both the text downloader and the image downloader, and the server can return the appropriate data for each downloader.\n\nFor example, I would like the following header element to be added to the request:\n\n```\n\n// string downloader\n\nrequest.SetRequestHeader(\"Accept\", \"text\");\n\n// or\n\nrequest.SetRequestHeader(\"X-VRCHAT-ACCEPT\", \"string\");\n\n```\n\n```\n\n// image downloader\n\nrequest.SetRequestHeader(\"Accept\", \"img\");\n\n// or\n\nrequest.SetRequestHeader(\"X-VRCHAT-ACCEPT\", \"image\");\n\n```",
  "error": null,
